│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause of the problem is that the model's output for       │
│ commit messages sometimes includes unuseful leading lines like     │
│ "Commit message:", "Got it, here is the commit message:", or       │
│ similar introductory text. These lines lead to noisy commit        │
│ messages that don't conform to the intended single commit message  │
│ line format.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ To address this, the best approach is to combine improvements in   │
│ the prompt and in post-processing:                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Enhance the commit_system prompt (prompts.commit_system) to     │
│    explicitly require JUST the commit message line, without any    │
│    extra introduction or trailing text. This reduces the           │
│    likelihood of the model including such text.                    │
│  2 Adjust the post-processing in GitRepo.get_commit_message to     │
│    detect and remove such leading lines. Often the model outputs   │
│    these phrases as a first line, then the real commit message     │
│    line starts from the next line or next non-empty line. By       │
│    stripping out known "introductory" lines and returning only the │
│    first "real" commit message line, we can improve the            │
│    cleanliness of the commit message.                              │
│                                                                    │
